    "result_text": "The build is green. The full test suite (`AcceptanceTest`, the only executable test class \u2014 `AcceptanceBase` is abstract and `AuditLogCapture` is a helper) passes.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented `namesakeCount` on owner creation: the number of existing owners (before this create) sharing the same `firstName` and `lastName`, compared case-insensitively.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `namesakeCount` integer property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` exposes it (and MapStruct maps it automatically).\n\n2. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 Added a `namesakeCount` field mapped to the `namesake_count` column, with getter/setter.\n\n3. **DB schemas** (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres`) \u2014 Added the `namesake_count` column to the `owners` table so the entity persists (hsqldb is what the tests use).\n\n4. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 Added `assignNamesakeCount(owner)`, called before `saveOwner`, which counts pre-existing owners matching first + last name case-insensitively (`equalsIgnoreCase`) and stores the result on the new owner. Because it runs before the insert, it counts only owners that existed before this create.\n\nThe value is persisted at creation and read back on `GET /api/owners/{id}`, matching the test's expectation of `namesakeCount == 1` for the second owner sharing a name with the first.",
